    "result": "I fixed it in `stats.go`, but I could not run the test. All the worker goroutines added to the same `Stats` value without a lock. That is a data race, and it drops increments, so the totals came out low and changed between runs.\n\nNow each worker counts into its own local `Stats`. When it finishes, it adds those counts to the shared total under a `sync.Mutex`. The number of workers is the same.\n\nMy commands to run tests and delete files were blocked. I added `stats_tmp_test.go`, which checks exact totals over 20 runs with 8 workers. Run `go test -race ./...` to check the fix. Then keep the test file, or rename or delete it.",
